From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexbob0 <190955252+Alexbob0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 10:07:40 +0100
Subject: Guest turns: only the guest's tools, no USER.md

BipAgents guest turns: a run or a session chat marked guest_turn {tools} (someone other than the agent's person
writes it) gets only those tools (MCP names + web_search), hidden from the list and refused in the dispatcher,
no USER.md, no context files, no memory writes or background review; its prompt is never stored.

Under the session authority the mark rides the durable api_turn_v1 admission (guest_turn, per admission, never a
session setting, part of the exact-retry identity) to the TurnRunner, which builds that turn an agent of its own,
never taken from nor put in the session's agent cache, and releases it after the turn.

BipAgents patch, documented in hermes/patches/README.md of the BipAgents repository.

Bip-Patch: 0018-guest-turns-closed-tools-no-user-profile
